{title: Days Of Elijah - Behold He Comes}
{key: G}
{x_theme: jubilee, praise, salvation}
{x_source: chrd:days_of_elijah_-_behold_he_comes.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
Be[Dsus]hold    [D]he   [G]comes, riding on the [C]clouds,
Shining like the [G]sun at the trumpet [D]call.
So [Dsus]lift    [D]your [G]voice, it's the year of jubi[C]lee,
And out of Zion's [G]hill, sal[D]vation [G]comes.

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]These are the days of Eli[C]jah,
De[G]claring the [D]word of the [G]Lord,
And [G]these are the days of Your ser[C]vant, Moses,
[G]Righteousness [D]being res[G]tored.
And [Bm]though these are days of great [Em]trials,
Of [C]famine and darkness and [D]sword,
Still, [G]we are the voice in the de[C]sert crying,
"Pre[Em7]pare ye the [D]way of the [G]Lord!"

{comment: Verse 2}
And [G]these are the days of Eze[C]kiel,
The [G]dry bones [D]becoming as [G]flesh.
And [G]these are the days of Your se[C]rvant, David,
Re[G]building the [D]temple of [G]praise.
And [Bm]these are the days of the har[Em]vest,
The [C]fields are as white in the [D]world.
And [G]we are the laborers [C]in Your vineyard,
De[Em]claring the [D]word of the [G]Lord!

{comment: Bridge}
{ci: (repeat 3x)}
[G]There is no God like Jehovah,  [C]there is no God like Jehovah,
[G]There is no God like Jehovah,  [D]there is no God like Jehovah.
